{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And called.</b> Now, he did not state their number. Some say two, but the correct view is many." "<b>Holy.</b> Three times, for thus they say continually. Similarly: היכל יהוה היכל יהוה היכל יהוה (Jeremiah 7:4); ארץ ארץ ארץ (ibid. 22:29)." "Holy is the attribute of the Name, and the holiness is in the essence and does not change with respect to places. And HaShem showed him this prophecy in order that he be sanctified from the impurity of the lips, for HaShem is holy, and so are His ministers and His emissaries." "And the meaning of <b>of hosts</b> is the angels, who are on high." "Even though He is holy, holy is His glory that fills the earth, which is below. And the one who explains 'fills all the earth' as 'those who dwell in it,' as in (Psalms 24:1) 'To YHWH the earth and its fullness' — has said nothing. And the proof: 'and the glory of YHWH filled all the earth.'"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:52:10.146596271Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}